WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.991
Week 1: How Spanish Works. spell a name recognize a stressed syllable build a sustainable study loop

2
00:00:06.991 --> 00:00:13.876
Cultural lens. Spanish is pluricentric: there is no single country that owns correct Spanish.

3
00:00:13.876 --> 00:00:25.947
Avoid the single-story trap. Treat country, region, age, relationship, and setting as variables. Describe the evidence you have without turning one example into a universal rule.

4
00:00:25.947 --> 00:00:37.805
Language variation. Recognize regional choices and ask what a form means locally. Use the neutral course model for production until the situation gives you a reason to adapt.

5
00:00:37.805 --> 00:00:46.805
Reflection. Compare this context with one you know. Name one similarity, one difference, and one question that would prevent an assumption.

6
00:00:46.805 --> 00:01:13.489
Model language. Mi nombre se escribe con cinco letras. — My name is spelled with five letters. La h no tiene sonido. — The letter h has no sound. Escucho y repito cada palabra. — I listen to and repeat every word. ¿Cuál es la sílaba tónica? — Which is the stressed syllable? La práctica breve y frecuente funciona mejor. — Brief, frequent practice works better.

7
00:01:13.489 --> 00:01:23.409
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
